##fileformat=VCFv4.3
##META=<ID=,Type=String,Number=.,Values=[A, B]>
##contig=<ID=chr1,length=1000000>
##CauseOfFailure=VCFv4.3.tex line 121: "All structured lines require an ID which must be unique within their type, i.e., within all the meta-information lines with the same `##key=` prefix." -- this ##META declaration's ID= attribute is present but empty, which the ID requirement is not satisfied by either. ##META's own required-ID rule is unconditional/version-independent (it has no pre-4.3 form at all) -- see DUPLICATE_METADATA_ID_HANDLING.md's "Missing ID is spec-grounded" section. See also that document's "Empty/whitespace ID is a deliberate stricter-than-bcftools choice" section: vcf-parser treats an empty ID= the same as a missing one, a deliberate editorial decision no spec version addresses.
##ExpectParser=warn
##Authority=VCFv4.3.tex line 121 (quoted above), plus DUPLICATE_METADATA_ID_HANDLING.md's "Empty/whitespace ID is a deliberate stricter-than-bcftools choice" section for why an empty ID is treated identically to a missing one even though bcftools itself does not (see below). ##fileformat=VCFv4.3 is required since ##META doesn't exist as a structured declaration type before VCFv4.3.
##Authority=bcftools 1.23.1 (htslib 1.23.1) keeps the declaration verbatim (ID=, unchanged) with NO warning at all, exit 0 -- BcftoolsDependencyTest#testMetaEmptyIdBcftoolsKeepsVerbatim pins this live measurement; re-confirmed directly via bcftools view -h on 2026-08-16. ##META isn't part of BCF's binary dictionary encoding, so htslib never validates its ID at all -- vcf-parser deliberately diverges from bcftools here, per the spec-grounded ID requirement (VCFv4.3.tex line 121).
